        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $\\frac{2}{25}\\int_{5}^{15}\\frac{{log}_{3}\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=\\frac{\\log{\\left(\\frac{x}{5} \\right)}}{\\log{\\left(3 \\right)}}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x \\log{\\left(3 \\right)}}\\,\u27f9\\,\\log{\\left(3 \\right)}\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $5$ | $15$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{25}\\int_{5}^{15}\\frac{{log}_{3}\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}{\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{25}\\int_{5}^{15}{log}_{3}\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{5}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\int_{0}^{1}u\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2 \\log{\\left(3 \\right)}}{5}\\int_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\operatorname{ln}3\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}\\right)|_{0}^{1} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\operatorname{ln}3\\cdot (\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2})\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}3}{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
